{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:33:42Z","created_by_operation":"op_b1922a57b4274f1ebedf36621839c849","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_78cb75480cd45010aff93a3de8eb72e5ac22eec06e46134cd5801b6ad765290d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"superseded","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"anomalyco/opencode@df23b7f9488a snapshot 62fba2c78cec8b3e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_6f8e3f04f51b3715524c0d8b3d56ee31bbfbe505a6c2120ba01f09ea457ace0c","slc_89aae9ac6a3976b67d991a58daadbd8ab0a54aca63213d65c48d616bb9175f9d","slc_b6cbf8aab77be1b75a86b440b0ffd578ecab25f95fc394ba410df8464340b9e8"],"source_ids":["src_f45e46cdb1725033a5de810b64cbcad3"],"text":"OpenCode ships two built-in primary agents switchable with the Tab key: build (default, full access) and plan (read-only, denies file edits and asks before bash commands), plus a general subagent invoked via @general.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:33:42Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b1922a57b4274f1ebedf36621839c849"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:33:42Z","created_by_operation":"op_b1922a57b4274f1ebedf36621839c849","evidence_type":"contextual_fact","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7f26c1b592ffbe2129326498d0d5cce2264b8fc21bcb9f65126676d220a41058","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"code-inspected","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"anomalyco/opencode@df23b7f9488a snapshot 62fba2c78cec8b3e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_10e6ba6df0a27698d12dfab01753f8bdab784e1cf6b9d82d89f70f0ae6ffb859"],"source_ids":["src_e0d83cbec32e5a5397fe3c37998b1556"],"text":"The agent module defines default permission rules: wildcard allow, ask for doom_loop and external directories, deny for question and plan transitions, and ask for reading .env files while allowing .env.example.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:57:56Z","updated_by_operation":"op_625d6526496849d087a88131eea300f8"}
